# Override pin (D4, every load) pressed for 20 s with a 1200 W surplus: the three loads are
# forced ON and CT2 measures their 3000 W, but a cycle with a forced load is not diverted energy:
# the firmware counts nothing while the forcing lasts, and counts again once released.
include common.scn
duration 70

at 0   -300
at 15  -300
at 15  1200   # load 1 fully on, load 2 partly
at 64  1200
at 64  -300   # surplus gone, before the last datalog line (every 5 s)

input 4 0 25  # forced...
input 4 1 45  # ...for 20 s

expect 22 pin 5 on
expect 22 pin 7 off
expect 30 pin 5 on    # forced
expect 30 pin 6 on
expect 30 pin 7 on
expect 60 pin 5 on
expect 60 pin 7 off
expect 68 pin 5 off
# Nothing counted during the forcing: the reported total does not move, and the lines whose
# datalog period lies within it report 0 W.
expect 27 47 diverted_wh 0 0
expect 28 42 diverted_w_avg 0 0
# Before and after: (1200 - 20) W x (10 s + 19 s) = 9.51 Wh, less the refill of the energy
# bucket the forced loads emptied (half its 3600 J, exported once released: 0.5 Wh), 9.01 Wh +-5 %.
# The firmware counts whole Wh: 8 or 9.
expect diverted_wh 8.56 9.46
